  "insights": [
   "JPM forecasts the federal budget deficit will widen to $2.06tn in FY27, up from $1.992tn in FY26, though it should edge lower as a share of GDP to 6.1%.",
   "A recovery in tariff receipts is a key assumption, with JPM expecting Section 301 and 232 actions to lift the average effective tariff rate to 13.8% in FY27 from 11.2% currently.",
   "Treasury faces a cumulative funding gap of approximately $1.6tn over FY27-28 under the current coupon auction schedule, making reliance on T-bills unsustainable.",
   "JPM expects Treasury to begin a multi-quarter series of nominal coupon auction size increases starting in August 2027, concentrated in 2s through 10s, TIPS, and FRNs.",
   "The T-bill share of marketable debt is expected to rise above 24% by YE27, with early signs of inelastic demand as bills have cheapened relative to SOFR.",
   "JPM expects 20- and 30-year auction sizes to remain unchanged through 2027, citing solid primary demand and healthy market functioning at the long end.",
   "JPM forecasts $2.226tn of net privately-held borrowing in 2027, with $1.011tn in bills and $1.036tn in coupons.",
   "There is a growing likelihood of a new 1-year SOFR-indexed FRN introduction in 2027, which JPM views as a superior product to the existing 2-year T-bill FRN.",
   "The WAM of marketable Treasury debt is projected to decline from 69 months currently to 68 months by YE27 and 67 months by YE28."
